        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(scheduler): prioritize exact-review backlog",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Adds durable exact-review queue pressure to background scheduling.\n- Keeps exact-review admission unchanged; it only reduces competing normal review, hot intake, and commit-review work.\n- Preserves an explicit commit-review page-size override while the exact queue is idle, while applying the protective cap when pressure is present.\n\n## Problem\n\nThe exact-review queue has its own 28-slot admission lane, independent of the 128-worker fleet budget. A full exact lane with a large pending backlog could therefore coexist with broad review planners receiving generous global-worker allowances. That increased competition for Codex, GitHub, and state publication while exact reviews were waiting.\n\n## Implementation\n\nThe scheduled sweep and commit-review planners read the public exact-review queue snapshot. The policy is intentionally conservative:\n\n- `idle`: no pending work, no valid capacity, or capacity is not full; existing scheduling applies.\n- `congested`: all exact slots are active and work is pending; broad review is capped at 16 workers.\n- `saturated`: all exact slots are active and at least one full exact lane is pending; broad review is capped at 4 workers.\n\nThe snapshot read is fail-open, so malformed or unavailable dashboard telemetry preserves the existing active-worker calculation. The caps are checked-in configuration values and are documented with the rest of the worker budget.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `pnpm run build:all`\n- `node --test test/repair/workflow-utils.test.ts` (48 passing)\n- `node --test --test-name-pattern \"background review schedulers yield\" test/sweep-workflow.test.ts`\n- `pnpm run lint:repair`\n- `pnpm run lint:scripts`\n- `pnpm run check:limits`\n- `pnpm exec oxfmt --check ...` for all changed code, workflow, config, and test files\n- `git diff --check`\n- `codex review --uncommitted` — clean after the commit-review override correction.\n- `codex review --base origin/main` — clean; no actionable defects.\n\nThe complete `test/sweep-workflow.test.ts` also has five unrelated local failures on this Windows host because its WSL Bash shim has no `/bin/bash`; the focused scheduler assertion passes.\n\n## Risks and rollout\n\n- This does not increase exact-review capacity or bypass per-target quotas; it only reduces competing background intake under sustained queue pressure.\n- The new queue read uses the existing public dashboard URL and adds no GitHub permissions or OAuth scopes.\n- The first live workflow run will emit a notice when it applies congestion or saturation throttling, making the selected policy visible in Actions logs.\n",
        "branch": "codex/csw-037-adaptive-review-priority",
